AI Use Level 2: Augmentative Usage Only
The goal of this policy is to allow students to use generative AI tools in their learning while retaining intellectual ownership and primary effort of their work. You are allowed to use generative AI tools to enhance or polish your work, but the main ideas and form of your work needs to be the result of your own effort. The specific usages that fit this principle will vary from course to course, and here are some potential permitted uses of generative AI tools in this course:
* brainstorming alternatives or options for an idea that you’ve developed yourself;
* seeking alternative explanations for course content to help you understand the material;
* performing a calculation or ancillary task, but not one that is novel and central to your idea;
* revising writing to improve clarity, grammar, or style but not to alter your own ideas;
* chatting with an AI chatbot to get answers to conceptual questions about course content;
* generating a quiz or practice problems to help you prepare for an exam;

